# Generated renders. The runners write full-length clips here; only the short
# gallery clips the README embeds are tracked, so name them rather than
# force-adding past a blanket ignore.
videos/**/*.mp4
videos/**/*.gif
# No exception for *_short.gif any more.
#
# The committed set is exactly what a published page embeds: the five gallery
# mosaics, which the README and the environment index carry. Everything else --
# the per-environment clips and the shorts the mosaics are built from -- is
# rendered by the docs-deploy workflow before it builds the site, so the
# repository does not carry tens of megabytes of regenerable media.
#
# The shorts were the exception because they were once what the environment
# pages embedded. They are not: ``scripts/generate_env_pages.py`` deliberately
# references ``pid_output.gif``, and keeping the shorts committed meant the
# repository carried 55 MB that nothing published referenced while the files
# the pages *did* reference were absent from a clean checkout.
.DS_Store
models

todo.md

training_videos*
*.csv
logs*
*.png
test_readme.py
*.zip
*.pdf

